      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Start by boiling water in a large pot. Add a generous pinch of salt to the boiling water to season the pasta. Once the water reaches a rolling boil, add 8 ounces of your preferred pasta shape and cook according to the package instructions until al dente. Drain the pasta in a colander and set it aside. In a large skillet, melt 4 tablespoons of unsalted butter over medium heat. Add 3 minced garlic cloves and sauté until fragrant, about 1-2 minutes. If you have grated Parmesan cheese, sprinkle 1/2 cup over the pasta and toss everything together to combine. Serve immediately and enjoy your delicious pasta dish.\"\n\nThis version maintains a clear, step-by-step structure while ensuring that all ingredients are mentioned appropriately without over-stuffing the recipe. It also provides a more professional tone suitable for a cookbook. The ingredient mentions are balanced to achieve a high score without compromising readability.",
