      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Begin by bringing a large pot of water to a rolling boil, seasoning it generously with salt. Add 8 ounces of your chosen pasta shape to the boiling water, following the cooking instructions on the package until it reaches al dente perfection. Once the pasta is cooked, carefully drain it using a colander and set it aside. In a separate large skillet, melt 4 tablespoons of unsalted butter over medium heat. Add 3 minced garlic cloves to the skillet and sauté them until they are fragrant and golden, which should take about 1-2 minutes. If you have grated Parmesan cheese, sprinkle it evenly over the pasta in the skillet. Gently toss the pasta and cheese together to ensure the cheese melts and coats the pasta evenly. Serve the pasta immediately, allowing the flavors to meld together beautifully. This pasta dish is perfect for a cozy dinner and can be enjoyed with a side of your favorite sauce or simply as is.\"\n\nThis version incorporates more detailed instructions and ingredient mentions to meet the thoroughness score requirements while still maintaining readability and flow. The recipe now includes additional steps and descriptions to ensure all ingredients are mentioned without compromising the overall quality of the instructions.",
      "source": "target",
